From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 23:52:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 057/106] ASoC: qcom: q6voice: default the vocproc Tx topology
 to passthrough

TX_SM_ECNS (the vendor's echo-canceller topology) running WITHOUT its
ACDB calibration outputs pure silence, while the sidetone - tapped before
Tx processing - stays audible locally: a perfectly ACKed call whose
uplink is dead, with the local mic even causing acoustic feedback on the
handset. The earlier "topology choice makes no difference" conclusion
was drawn while every call was silent because of the mismatched CVD
session name, so that comparison was invalid.

Default Tx to VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE (bypass) and expose both
topologies as runtime-writable module parameters for A/B testing between
calls. Switch Tx back to ECNS only once real vocproc calibration loading
works.

Verified on real VoLTE calls on sm7150 (surya): with ECNS the far end
hears nothing, with NONE the mic audio arrives fine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
index 63f77b56d..df239c68f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
@@ -106,6 +106,29 @@ struct vss_ivocproc_cmd_create_full_control_session_v2_cmd {
 	char name[20];
 } __packed;
 
+/*
+ * Vocproc topologies, runtime-tunable for A/B testing between calls
+ * (/sys/module/q6cvp/parameters/{tx,rx}_topology, read at session create,
+ * i.e. at call setup).
+ *
+ * Tx defaults to VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE (passthrough), NOT the
+ * vendor's TX_SM_ECNS: the echo-canceller running WITHOUT its ACDB
+ * calibration outputs pure silence, while the sidetone (tapped before Tx
+ * processing) stays audible locally - a perfectly ACKed call whose uplink
+ * is dead. Verified on a real call: with ECNS the far end hears nothing,
+ * with NONE the mic reaches it fine. The earlier "topology makes no
+ * difference" conclusion predated the CVD session-name fix, when every
+ * call was silent for that unrelated reason - it was invalid. Switch Tx
+ * back to 0x10F71 only once real vocproc calibration loading works.
+ */
+static uint tx_topology = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE;
+module_param(tx_topology, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tx_topology, "Vocproc Tx topology ID (0x10F70=none/passthrough)");
+
+static uint rx_topology = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_RX_DEFAULT;
+module_param(rx_topology, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_topology, "Vocproc Rx topology ID (0x10F70=none/passthrough)");
+
 struct q6voice_session *q6cvp_session_create(enum q6voice_path_type path,
 					     u16 tx_port, u16 rx_port)
 {
@@ -114,16 +137,8 @@ struct q6voice_session *q6cvp_session_create(enum q6voice_path_type path,
 	cmd.hdr.pkt_size = sizeof(cmd);
 	cmd.hdr.opcode = VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_CREATE_FULL_CONTROL_SESSION_V2;
 
-	/*
-	 * The stock topologies (echo cancellation on Tx, the default
-	 * processing chain on Rx) create and enable the vocproc without any
-	 * error, same as VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE - a passthrough
-	 * topology needs no more calibration than these do for a call to
-	 * come up. Nothing about topology choice makes the difference between
-	 * a silent and a working call, so keep the vendor's actual choice.
-	 */
-	cmd.tx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_TX_SM_ECNS;
-	cmd.rx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_RX_DEFAULT;
+	cmd.tx_topology_id = tx_topology;
+	cmd.rx_topology_id = rx_topology;
 
 	cmd.direction = VSS_IVOCPROC_DIRECTION_RX_TX;
 	cmd.tx_port_id = tx_port;
@@ -132,7 +147,15 @@ struct q6voice_session *q6cvp_session_create(enum q6voice_path_type path,
 	cmd.vocproc_mode = VSS_IVOCPROC_VOCPROC_MODE_EC_INT_MIXING;
 	cmd.ec_ref_port_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_PORT_ID_NONE;
 
-	return q6voice_session_create(Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVP, path, &cmd.hdr);
+	{
+		struct q6voice_session *s;
+
+		s = q6voice_session_create(Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVP, path, &cmd.hdr);
+		if (!IS_ERR(s))
+			dev_info(s->dev, "vocproc topologies tx=0x%x rx=0x%x\n",
+				 tx_topology, rx_topology);
+		return s;
+	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6cvp_session_create);
 
